  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(i) Fittig&nbsp;reaction:&nbsp;Aryl halides give analogous compounds when treated with sodium in dry ether, in which two aryl groups are joined together. It is called Fittig reaction.</p><p>(ii)&nbsp;Wurtz-Fittig reaction:&nbsp;A mixture of an alkyl halide and aryl halide gives an alkylarene when treated with sodium in dry ether and is called Wurtz-Fittig reaction.</p><p>(iii)&nbsp;Finkelstein reaction: Alkyl iodides are often prepared by the reaction of alkyl chlorides/ bromides with NaI in dry acetone. This reaction is known as Finkelstein reaction.</p><p>(iv) Sandmeyer reaction:&nbsp;When a primary aromatic amine, dissolved or suspended in cold aqueous mineral acid, is treated with sodium nitrite, a diazonium salt is formed. Mixing the solution of freshly prepared diazonium salt with cuprous chloride or cuprous bromide results in the replacement of the diazonium group by &ndash;Cl or &ndash;Br</p><p>Hence, the correct matching is given in the below table:</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\" rowspan=\"1\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>List I</strong></td>\t\t\t<td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>List II</strong></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>A</td>\t\t\t<td>\t\t\t<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t\t\t\t<tbody>\t\t\t\t\t<tr>\t\t\t\t\t\t<td><img src=\"assets\\qt0061_3727122f4364.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 140px;\" /></td>\t\t\t\t\t</tr>\t\t\t\t</tbody>\t\t\t</table>\t\t\t</td>\t\t\t<td>\t\t\t<p>Wurtz Fitting reaction</p>\t\t\t</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>B</td>\t\t\t<td><img src=\"assets\\qt0061_51e0a578f5a9.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 117px;\" /></td>\t\t\t<td>Fitting reaction</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>C</td>\t\t\t<td><img src=\"assets\\qt0061_aa1da9737c4d.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 144px;\" /></td>\t\t\t<td>\t\t\t<p>Sandmeyer reaction</p>\t\t\t</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>D</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>Cl</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>NaI</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>Nacl</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td>Finkelstein reaction</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table>"
